# CI Test Secret Allowlist
# ========================
# Regex patterns (one per line) for secret values that are safe to hardcode
# in CI-only contexts (GitHub Actions workflows, docker-compose.test.yml, etc.).
#
# The pre-commit hook checks each staged line containing a known secret name
# (JWT_ACCESS_SECRET, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET, etc.) against these patterns. If the
# VALUE side of the line matches any pattern here, the line is skipped.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# To add a new CI-only test value, append a regex that matches it.
# Keep patterns as specific as possible to avoid accidentally allowlisting
# real secrets.

# --- smoke_* prefixed values (all-in-one Docker smoke tests) ---
smoke_
smoke_jwt_access_secret
smoke_jwt_refresh_secret

# --- ci-flagchain prefixed values (admin→gateway flag-chain container tests) ---
ci-flagchain

# --- test-* and test_* prefixed values ---
^test[-_]secret
^test[-_]jwt
^test[-_]gateway
